A bit of debug-mode testing gives the following minimum fail rates at
an 18 natural spellcasting stat:
"naked" - 31%
+1 or better helm of brilliance - 30%
gauntlets of power - 85%
gauntlets of power and +1 or better helm of brilliance - 84%
robe - 0%
robe, gauntlets of power - 4%
robe, gauntlets of power, helm of brilliance - 3%

>  I got my int up to 12 from eating a mind
> flayer, but 12 is just not enough to cast any spell reliably,

For a valkyrie, intelligence will help reading spellbooks, but it will
_not_ improve fail rates. The valkyrie's "casting stat" is wisdom. 18
wisdom without special equipment gives 31% minimum fail, unless the
spell is the valkyrie's special spell, cone of cold, or an "emergency"
spell like healing (lower min. fail in both cases).

> take off my GoP.  A nice HoB might help this.

Not likely, unless your wisdom is below 18 currently. 19 is max.
effective wisdom as far as minimum fail is concerned, getting more
won't help much.

If you want to get better fail rates for low-level spells like magic
missile, your only hope is a robe. 

